# Swim water below the surface row (TileKind::Swim, D-076): clear T with
# a slow shimmering t caustic net (cell points circle by 1 px over the 4
# frames), tileable in x and y, so any depth of water stacks without
# bands. Stays teal (no b/B), so the pale lake bed reads through it and
# it never looks like the dark lethal tile_wolfgangsee_water_deep.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids are the source.
sprite = tile_see_wasser_tief
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = idle frames=4 ticks=16 loop
